    "title": "The exact m-dependent 2-adic valuation law for coefficients of the Thue-Morse power T(x)^m",
    "description": "Let T(x) = prod_{k>=0} (1 - x^{2^k}) and T(x)^m = sum t_m(n) x^n. The commonly guessed formula nu_2(t_m((m-1)n+j)) = (m-1) ceil(nu_2(n+1)/2) - ((m-1)/4)(nu_2(n+1) mod 2) is correct only for m=5; for m=9 the valuation is block-constant but equals floor((5 nu_2(n+1) + (nu_2(n+1) mod 2))/2). Conjecture: for each odd m ≡ 1 (mod 4) there is a piecewise-linear function Phi_m of v = nu_2(n+1), with slope determined by the number of even low-order binomial coefficients of (1-x)^m (equivalently the Kummer carry pattern of m), giving nu_2(t_m((m-1)n+j)) on the sub-blocks where block-constancy holds. Approach: use the coefficient form of T(x)^m = (1-x)^m T(x^2)^m to derive a linear recursion, then analyze 2-adic cancellation of leading terms by strong induction on the 2-adic level; validate against m = 13, 17, 21.",
